# Panel

Use a panel for a significant completion or a deliberate interruption in a journey.

These are civica.uk reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## When to use it

Use a confirmation panel after a whole setup task completes, with the next step nearby. An interruption panel may pause a process when the user needs important context before continuing.

## When not to use it

Do not use large panels as decoration inside ordinary help text, or show a success panel for every light switch. A recurring dashboard reading belongs in a card or summary.

## Home Assistant adaptation

A dashboard import confirmation should state exactly what was imported and where to find it. Do not say “Backup restored” until the owning restore operation confirms completion. An interruption must explain its consequence without inventing authority or demanding an unnecessary approval.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Use a short heading and readable supporting text. Keep next actions outside the coloured area where that produces clearer focus and contrast. Ensure meaning survives without the fill colour and avoid large uppercase headings.

